  -- Proof comment: this is the closed-fiber Nakayama bridge. The intended route is to identify
  -- `κ(p) ⊗[R] M` with the closed fiber of `M_p`, lift residue generators through the quotient map,
  -- and then apply `span_eq_top_of_residue_quotient_span_eq_top`; the reverse direction sends
  -- chosen local generators to the quotient and bounds the fiber dimension by the surjective
  -- linear-combination map from `κ(p)^k`.
